# Revnote — Docker build context filter (repository root is the build context).
#
# The API image is built from the REPOSITORY ROOT because it is a uv workspace:
# the build needs the root `pyproject.toml`, the single root `uv.lock`, and the
# `apps/api` member. Everything else is excluded to keep the context small and,
# more importantly, to guarantee no local secret or Python/Node artefact can be
# baked into a published image.
#
# Keep in sync with apps/api/Dockerfile: the paths it COPYs must stay un-ignored:
#   pyproject.toml, uv.lock, .python-version, apps/api/{pyproject.toml,src,
#   alembic.ini,migrations,README.md}

# ------------------------------- secrets ---------------------------------- #
# Never ship credentials. `.env.example` is excluded too: the image must start
# from the process environment only, with no dotenv file present at runtime.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
secrets/

# ------------------------------- version control -------------------------- #
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# --------------------------------- Python --------------------------------- #
# Any local virtualenv must not leak into the image (the image builds its own).
.venv/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
build/
**/build/
dist/
**/dist/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# ------------------------------ Node / web -------------------------------- #
# The API image never needs the Web app or its dependency tree. Root workspace
# metadata for pnpm is excluded too — uv does not read it.
apps/web/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/dist-ssr/
pnpm-lock.yaml
pnpm-workspace.yaml
package.json
.npmrc

# --------------------------------- tooling -------------------------------- #
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.log
tmp/
temp/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ----------------------------------- docs --------------------------------- #
# Not needed to build or run the API. (`apps/api/README.md` is intentionally
# NOT excluded — the package metadata references its own README.)
docs/
build-prompt.md
plan-prompt.md
**/*.md
!apps/api/README.md

# -------------------------------- compose --------------------------------- #
# Compose files are for local infrastructure only; they are not needed in an
# image and would otherwise shadow nothing useful.
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.override.yml
.dockerignore
apps/api/Dockerfile
